{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (Task ID #5177) to implement srd005-wc R2.1-R2.4 (flag selection and output formatting) for the `cmd/wc` utility in a Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: `-l` flag must count newline characters\n   - R2.2: `-w` flag must count words (maximal sequences of non-whitespace using unicode.IsSpace)\n   - R2.3: `-c` flag must count bytes; `-c` and `-m` are mutually exclusive in output, `-m` takes precedence when both given\n   - R2.4: `-m` flag must count characters (Unicode code points/runes); invalid UTF-8 bytes count as one character each\n   \n   Files to create/modify: `cmd/wc/main.go` and `cmd/wc/wc_test.go`\n   Acceptance criteria: R2.1-R2.4 implemented, differential tests added, `go test ./cmd/wc/... -count=1` passes, `go vet ./cmd/wc/...` reports no issues.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gwc`) via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling: all cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - LC_ALL=C: all differential tests must set this for locale-independent comparison\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary for testing\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gwc\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max per function (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - Write all files before building/testing (implementation strat